  "question": {
    "text": "If \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) are \\(2 \\times 2\\) matrices, then which of the following is true?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\\((\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{B})^2=\\mathrm{A}^2+\\mathrm{B}^2+2 \\mathrm{AB}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\((A-B)^2=A^2+B^2-2 A B\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\((A-B)(A+B)=A^2+A B-B A-B^2\\)",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\\((A-B)(A+B)=A^2-B^2\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "For two \\(2 \\times 2\\) matrices, \\(A ~\\&~ B\\)\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& (A-B) \\times(A+B) \\\\\n& =A \\times A+A \\times B-B \\times A-B \\times B \\\\\n& =A^2-B^2+A B-B A\n\\end{aligned}\\)\nHence, \\((A-B)(A+B)=A^2+A B-B A-B^2\\)"
  }
}